# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in your own values.
# backend/.env is git-ignored -- never commit real credentials.
#
# This one file holds settings for TWO independent subsystems, each
# reading only the keys that are theirs:
#   - app/core/config.py's Settings (the FastAPI app) reads ONLY
#     MLCOPILOT_-prefixed variables, via pydantic-settings.
#   - backend/langgraph/llm/model.py (the LLM client) reads
#     OPENAI_API_KEY (and MLCOPILOT_OPENAI_MODEL) directly via
#     os.getenv(), independent of Settings.
# See app/core/config.py's module docstring for why that separation
# exists and how Settings tolerates this file holding both without
# either weakening its own validation or requiring two separate files.

# --- backend/langgraph/llm/model.py (the LLM client) ---
# Required for the /copilot/* endpoints and any LLM-backed graph test.
# langchain-openai's ChatOpenAI reads this exact variable name.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the default model used by get_chat_model().
# MLCOPILOT_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- app/core/config.py's Settings (the FastAPI app) ---
# All optional -- shown here with their defaults. Uncomment to override.
# A typo in one of these (e.g. MLCOPILOT_DATABSE_URL) will raise a clear
# error at startup rather than being silently ignored -- see
# app/core/config.py's `_check_for_prefix_typos()`.
# MLCOPILOT_APP_NAME=ML Copilot API
# MLCOPILOT_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
# MLCOPILOT_CORS_ORIGINS=["http://localhost:3000"]
# MLCOPILOT_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./app.db
# MLCOPILOT_STORAGE_DIR=storage/datasets
